%N A398767 a(n) is the number of grid points in an n X n X n cube that cannot be connected by a straight line to a given corner without passing through another grid point.
%C A398767 These are the grid points which are not visible when looking from a given corner of an n X n X n cube.
%C A398767 Let the given corner be O at (0,0,0) and any grid point be P at (x,y,z). A straight line from O to P will not pass through another grid point if and only if gcd(x,y,z) = 1.
%H A398767 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A398767/b398767.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a> (terms 1..200 from Janaka Rodrigo).
%H A398767 Janaka Rodrigo, <a href="/A398767/a398767.txt">Python code of A398767</a>
%F A398767 a(n) = (n+1)^3 - A090025(n) - 1.
%e A398767 a(3) = (3+1)^2 - A090025(3) - 1 = 64 - 49 - 1 = 14.
%e A398767 Coordinates of the grid points which cannot directly connect to (0,0,0) without passing through another grid point are: (0,2,0), (0,3,0), (0,0,2), (0,2,2), (0,0,3), (0,3,3), (2,0,0), (2,2,0), (2,0,2), (2,2,2), (3,0,0), (3,3,0),(3,0,3), (3,3,3).
%t A398767 A398767[n_] := -Sum[MoebiusMu[k]*((Quotient[n, k] + 1)^3 - 1), {k, 2, n}];
%t A398767 Array[A398767, 50] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Nov 11 2026 *)
%Y A398767 Cf. A090025.
%K A398767 nonn,new
%O A398767 1,2
